\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Transverse intensity patterns $|U_{lm}|^2$ of Hermite--Gaussian modes $\mathrm  {TEM}_{lm}$ (the labels give $lm$). The first index $l$ counts the dark nodal lines along $x$ and the second index $m$ along $y$, so $\mathrm  {TEM}_{00}$ is a single spot, $\mathrm  {TEM}_{10}$ has two lobes side by side, and $\mathrm  {TEM}_{33}$ has a $4\times 4$ array of lobes. The pattern grows with the order, as stated after Eq.~\eqref  {eq:hg}. Source: Le Mans Universit\'e course (F.~Varet), \url  {https://perso.univ-lemans.fr/~fvaret/opi/cours_maj/OPI_ang_M01_C03_web_gen_auroraW/co/Contenu_13.html}.}}{11}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hgmodes}{{7}{11}{Transverse intensity patterns $|U_{lm}|^2$ of Hermite--Gaussian modes $\mathrm {TEM}_{lm}$ (the labels give $lm$). The first index $l$ counts the dark nodal lines along $x$ and the second index $m$ along $y$, so $\mathrm {TEM}_{00}$ is a single spot, $\mathrm {TEM}_{10}$ has two lobes side by side, and $\mathrm {TEM}_{33}$ has a $4\times 4$ array of lobes. The pattern grows with the order, as stated after Eq.~\eqref {eq:hg}. Source: Le Mans Universit\'e course (F.~Varet), \url {https://perso.univ-lemans.fr/~fvaret/opi/cours_maj/OPI_ang_M01_C03_web_gen_auroraW/co/Contenu_13.html}}{figure.caption.15}{}}
